tasks.details:
Add a BREX self-consistency lint pass that runs over a BREX before it is used:
- every objectPath compiles;
- every structureObjectRule has an objectUse;
- allowedObjectFlag="2" rules actually carry objectValue children (18 in these three BREX do not, and are silently no-ops);
- valueForm="pattern" values are valid XSD regexes;
- valueForm="range" values parse as a range or set;
- @brSeverityLevel values exist in the severity-level file;
- duplicate structureObjectRule/@id and duplicate brDecisionIdentNumber.

Implemented in acd/brex_checker.py as BrexChecker.lint_brex(brex_path), a standalone opt-in method (no equivalent in s1kd-brexcheck) meant to be called on a BREX file before passing it to override_brex_list/set_brex_path, independent of any checked object. Reuses _get_object_rule_nodes(brex_path, schema=None) to walk every structureObjectRule/objrule regardless of rulesContext, so both modern and S1000D <= 3.0 legacy-spelling rules are linted. Each of the seven checks is its own finding category (InvalidXPath, MissingObjectUse, EmptyValueFlag2, InvalidPattern, InvalidRange, UnknownSeverityLevel, DuplicateId, DuplicateBrDecisionIdentNumber): XPath compilation reuses elementpath.Selector the same way the checker itself does; pattern validity reuses translate_xsd_regex_to_python plus regex.compile(..., V1); range/set validity checks for empty members/bounds in the ~/| grammar is_in_set/is_in_range otherwise silently mis-parse instead of rejecting; the severity check resolves a rule's own brSeverityLevel or the BREX root's defaultBrSeverityLevel against the checker's currently configured .brseveritylevels table (_get_severity_levels) and is skipped entirely when none is configured/discoverable, since there is nothing to validate against; duplicate @id/brDecisionIdentNumber are tallied across the whole file and reported once each with every occurrence's line number. Verified end-to-end against all 7 bundled default BREX in acd/brex/: zero findings on the BREX with no value-only flag-2 rules, and exactly 18 EmptyValueFlag2 findings on the F/G/H issues (20 on the E issue) — matching the evidence base's "18 in these three BREX do not [carry objectValue]" figure exactly, with no false positives from the pattern/range/severity/duplicate checks against real production rule data. Covered by tests/test_brex_lint.py: a clean BREX with no findings, each of the eight finding categories individually (including the legacy objrule/objpath/objuse/objval spelling for the pattern check), a flag-1 rule with no objectValue correctly not flagged, valid set/range values not flagged, a known severity level not flagged, and the severity check skipped when no .brseveritylevels file is configured.
